This product includes software developed as part of the DeepSIF project
(https://github.com/bfinl/DeepSIF), Copyright (c) 2022, authors of DeepSIF,
released under the Clear BSD License. The neural mass model simulation and
forward modelling pipeline in forward/ is derived from that work; individual
files note this in their headers.

  Sun R, Sohrabpour A, Worrell GA, He B. Deep neural networks constrained by
  neural mass models improve electrophysiological source imaging of
  spatiotemporal brain dynamics. Proc Natl Acad Sci. 2022;119(31):e2201128119.
  doi:10.1073/pnas.2201128119

The simulation pipeline builds on The Virtual Brain, which is distributed
separately under its own license and is not redistributed here:

  Sanz Leon P, Knock SA, Woodman MM, et al. The Virtual Brain: a simulator of
  primate brain network dynamics. Front Neuroinformatics. 2013;7.
  doi:10.3389/fninf.2013.00010

Source dynamics are generated with the Jansen-Rit neural mass model:

  Jansen BH, Rit VG. Electroencephalogram and visual evoked potential generation
  in a mathematical model of coupled cortical columns. Biol Cybern.
  1995;73(4):357-366. doi:10.1007/BF00199471

